{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,25]],"date-time":"2026-02-25T19:37:57Z","timestamp":1772048277867,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":15,"publisher":"American Geophysical Union (AGU)","issue":"2","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2003,1,24]],"date-time":"2003-01-24T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1043366400000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":23,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Geophysical Research Letters"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2003,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>The realization of the International Terrestrial Reference System (ITRS) for 2000 (ITRF2000), provides an accurate estimation of relative motions for 6 major tectonic plates. In order to comply with the ITRS specification, a No\u2010Net\u2010Rotation Condition (NNRC) was applied by aligning the orientation time evolution of the ITRF2000 to that of the geophysical model NNR\u2010NUVEL\u20101A. This implicit application of the NNRC, since the NNR\u2010NUVEL\u20101A satisfies that condition, is achieved by using a consistent geodetic method, minimizing the global rotation rate between the ITRF2000 and the NNR\u2010NUVEL\u20101A model. The main focus of this paper is to examine how the ITRF2000 satisfies this condition by computing rotation rate components with respect to the Tisserand frame which is the basis of the NNRC. Numerical tests based on several approaches illustrate the sensitivity of the alignment to NNR\u2010NUVEL\u20101A and they also show that the ITRF2000 is aligned at the 1 mm\/yr level.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1029\/2002gl016279","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2003,5,23]],"date-time":"2003-05-23T18:26:56Z","timestamp":1053714416000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":35,"title":["The impact of a No\u2010Net\u2010Rotation Condition on ITRF2000"],"prefix":"10.1029","volume":"30","author":[{"given":"Zuheir","family":"Altamimi","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Institut G\u00e9ographique National  Paris France"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Patrick","family":"Sillard","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Institut G\u00e9ographique National  Paris France"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Claude","family":"Boucher","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Institut G\u00e9ographique National  Paris France"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"13","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2003,1,24]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_7_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","DOI":"10.1029\/2001JB000561","article-title":"ITRF2000: A New Release of the International Terrestrial Reference Frame for Earth Science Applications","author":"Altamimi Z.","year":"2002","journal-title":"J Geophys. Res."},{"key":"e_1_2_7_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"278","DOI":"10.1029\/EO082i025p00273-01","article-title":"The Terrestrial Reference Frame and the Dynamic Earth","volume":"82","author":"Altamimi Z.","year":"2001","journal-title":"Eos Trans AGU"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/91GL01532"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/978-94-009-0933-5_15"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1111\/j.1365-246X.1990.tb06579.x"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/94GL02118"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_8_1","volume-title":"Global Reference Frames: Connecting Observation to Theory and Geodesy to Geophysics","author":"Dermanis A.","year":"2001"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_9_1","first-page":"377","volume-title":"in IAG Symposia","author":"Drewes H.","year":"1998"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_10_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/2001GL013232"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_11_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/97JB00514"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_12_1",